{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfmtg3Xrz5CJsqbU2Bzoe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Outcome: APPROVE, 1 row. TC-329 is now Approved and anchored.**\n\n**Why TC-329 was ready:**\n- **Against LLR-270:** Its Method checks each of LLR-270's new first-mint rules with an observable assertion:\n  - Two first calls at once give one mint and one unretained call that states its reason.\n  - Before launch the record holds only family, route id and lease; after bookkeeping it holds generation 1, the minted id and active state, with no lease.\n  - A crashed first call's lease-only record is retired as `lease expired unreleased`.\n  - A late mint records `store moved on` and leaves the newer record alone, whether the call that took over is still running or has finished.\n  - A first mint that raises leaves neither record nor tombstone.\n  - At dial zero, no store is written.\n- **Against the other test cases:** It doesn't overlap TC-266, TC-267 or TC-268.\n- **Against the code:** All five evidence tests exist in `tests/test_session_keep.py` and assert what the Method says.\n- **One check I made:** a lease-only record's tombstone is applied through the same `load_honoured` → `_apply_tombstone` path whether it runs at once or later when the store lock is held. TC-329 drives the immediate case and TC-267 already covers the deferred one, so nothing in LLR-270's first-mint text goes untested.\n\n**Commits, each with the `WI: WI-838` trailer:**\n- `55dfc1d2`: the verdict, at `docs/reviews/wi-838-first-mint-takes-a-lease/003-ADJUDICATE-6e89a27.md`.\n- `281eee2b`: the approval. It flips TC-329's `status` from `Drafted` to `Approved`, the only registry change. It includes the snapshot from `intake.py snapshot --approves \"docs/test/test-cases.toml=WI-838\"`, which went through without a refusal and recorded act 43 with `approved = [\"TC-329\"]`.\n\nI approved only TC-329, the one row marked as mine; every other row in the chain was already Approved and I left it unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":104826,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433},"output_tokens":703,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2584b99b-5c67-48ab-94cc-44374d289363","uuid":"7c7c9023-3f20-4675-a234-188c698adc64","timestamp":"2026-10-06T23:59:17.503Z","request_id":"req_011Cfmtg35qVGsaMTQ8K4QHe"}
